cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Quantum Canary, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Quantum Canary"
abstract: >-
  Qubit health checks for IBM superconducting and IonQ trapped-ion hardware.
  On IBM, from 74 single-qubit probe circuits (8,640 shots per qubit) in one
  short job, Quantum Canary estimates T1, T2, T2*, the frequency offset and the
  single-qubit gate error; on IonQ it estimates the gate error by randomized
  benchmarking. Every estimate has an uncertainty, every fit is checked against
  its noise model, every qubit gets a health status, and checks can be compared
  to detect changes.
authors:
  - given-names: Kanishka
    family-names: Singh
    affiliation: "Joint Quantum Institute, University of Maryland"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9611-1615"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/singh-kishu257/quantum-canary"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - qubit characterization
  - randomized benchmarking
  - drift detection
  - superconducting qubits
  - trapped ions
